1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,938
At E3 in 1995, Sega announced the Saturn.

2
00:00:04,948 --> 00:00:07,767
$399, in stores that day.

3
00:00:07,927 --> 00:00:10,681
Later that day, Sony's Steve Race walked up to

4
00:00:10,691 --> 00:00:11,340
the podium.

5
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:12,860
He said one thing.

6
00:00:12,870 --> 00:00:15,127
"$299." Then he sat back down.

7
00:00:15,287 --> 00:00:17,889
The PlayStation was a hundred dollars cheaper.

8
00:00:18,049 --> 00:00:21,131
Sega's boss later admitted they didn't have enough stock,

9
00:00:21,141 --> 00:00:21,996
or enough games.

10
00:00:22,156 --> 00:00:25,402
The PlayStation went on to sell more than 100

11
00:00:25,412 --> 00:00:29,153
million, and by 2001, Sega had quit making consoles.
